This file marks the lensing FRAMEWORK checkout (the "mother" repo).

tools/package.py never ships it, so its presence means: you are in the
framework, not in an instance. tools/lensing_guard.py reads it to
(a) disable the instance gates here, so framework development is unimpeded,
and (b) refuse `/bootstrap` in place.

A new project is instantiated as its OWN folder holding a full copy:

    zig build package                 # -> dist/lensing.tar.gz
    tar xzf dist/lensing.tar.gz -C /path/to/projects
    cd /path/to/projects/lensing      # rename it; then /bootstrap

Cloning this repository is NOT an instantiation path: the clone carries this
marker, has no .lensing-upstream.json provenance manifest, and bootstrap will
refuse to run in it.
